[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63794,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrial stromal nodule is a well-circumscribed endometrial stromal tumour resembling proliferative-phase endometrial stroma and lacking lymphovascular invasion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63795,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8930/0 Endometrial stromal nodule</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63796,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E88 &amp; XH8C13 Benign endometrial stromal nodule &amp; Endometrial stromal nodule</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63797,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> benign endometrial stromal tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63798,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63799,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are localized within the uterus; they may be submucosal, intramural, or (rarely) subserosal.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63800,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may present with abnormal uterine bleeding, abdominal pain, enlarged uterus, or a pelvic mass {2327549; 7793473; 11979087; 7216172}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63801,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrial stromal nodule is a rare tumour {2327549; 7793473; 11979087; 7216172}. It occurs more often in perimenopausal women (mean patient age: 53&nbsp;years; range:&nbsp;23&ndash;86&nbsp;years).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63802,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63803,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 70% of tumours with classic histology, as well as some tumours with smooth muscle or sex cord differentiation, harbour t(7;17)(p21;q15) resulting in <em>JAZF1</em>-<em>SUZ12</em> fusion {11371647; 17667554; 15043312; 21836477}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63804,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are well circumscribed, solid, and yellow to tan, with a mean size of 7&nbsp;cm (range: 1&ndash;22&nbsp;cm). They may be polypoid or may show cystic change {2327549; 7793473; 11979087; 7216172}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63805,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are circumscribed or at most may have &le;&nbsp;3&nbsp;finger-like projections &lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;mm from the margin. They are typically densely cellular, displaying uniform small cells with scant cytoplasm (except if decidualized), round to oval nuclei, and inconspicuous nucleoli that may whorl around arterioles (which may be hyalinized). Scattered large vessels may be seen at the tumour periphery. Mitotic activity is usually low but if increased does not exclude this diagnosis. Collagen bands, foamy histiocytes, and less commonly cholesterol clefts may be present. Variant morphology includes smooth muscle differentiation {17667554; 15043312}, fibromyxoid change (hypocellular appearance), sex cord&ndash;like differentiation (including retiform), endometrioid glands, and rhabdoid or epithelioid morphology {2327549; 11979087; 7216172; 10542938; 11781523; 19236513; 9689655}. The immunoprofile mirrors that reported for low-grade endometrial stromal sarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63806,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63807,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63808,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a well-demarcated nodule; tumour cells reminiscent of proliferative-type stroma; no lymphovascular invasion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63809,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63810,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients have excellent outcomes, providing the tumour interface with myometrium is well sampled to exclude sarcoma {11979087; 2327549; 7793473; 7216172}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:03:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]